From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 02:35:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] spi: geni-qcom: Let the core complete successful GPI messages

The GPI DMA completion callback writes zero to the current SPI message
status when one transfer succeeds. The SPI core sees a status other than
-EINPROGRESS and stops processing the message before it accounts for the
transfer or starts any later transfer. A 238592-byte IR waveform sent on
Piano completes successfully but spi_message_done reports zero bytes.

Set the message status only on a DMA error or a nonzero residue. Always
wake the core for the current transfer. The core then accounts for each
successful transfer, handles chip-select transitions and completes the
whole message. The existing error and DMA termination paths still apply.

The linked QSPI proposal also leaves status unchanged on success, as part
of converting the driver to own the entire message. This fix keeps the
existing transfer_one() model and the core's message handling.

Fixes: 74b86d6af81b ("spi: qcom: geni: set the error code for gpi transfer")
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/linux-spi/20261106-qspi_upstream_series-v1-1-21f43042dd60@oss.qualcomm.com/
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
---
 drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c | 20 ++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c b/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
index a5f99338c..6f947d120 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
@@ -463,20 +463,16 @@ spi_gsi_callback_result(void *cb, const struct dmaengine_result *result)
 	struct spi_controller *spi = cb;
 	struct spi_geni_master *mas = spi_controller_get_devdata(spi);
 
-	spi->cur_msg->status = -EIO;
-	if (result->result != DMA_TRANS_NOERROR) {
-		dev_err(&spi->dev, "DMA txn failed: %d\n", result->result);
+	if (result->result != DMA_TRANS_NOERROR || result->residue) {
+		spi->cur_msg->status = -EIO;
+		if (result->result != DMA_TRANS_NOERROR)
+			dev_err(&spi->dev, "DMA txn failed: %d\n", result->result);
+		else
+			dev_err(&spi->dev, "DMA xfer has pending: %u\n", result->residue);
 		trace_geni_se_regs(&mas->se);
-		spi_finalize_current_transfer(spi);
-		return;
-	}
-
-	if (!result->residue) {
-		spi->cur_msg->status = 0;
-		dev_dbg(&spi->dev, "DMA txn completed\n");
 	} else {
-		dev_err(&spi->dev, "DMA xfer has pending: %d\n", result->residue);
-		trace_geni_se_regs(&mas->se);
+		/* Leave completion of the whole message to the SPI core. */
+		dev_dbg(&spi->dev, "DMA txn completed\n");
 	}
 
 	spi_finalize_current_transfer(spi);
